In this paper, we deal with a singular elliptic system of Kirchhoff type equations, specifically the equation given by

\begin{align*}
\begin{cases}
&\delta_{p}(t\,(t^{-\alpha}(|\Delta_{\sigma}u|^{2p-2})^{\frac{1}{p}})^{p-2})\Delta_{\sigma}u+|u|^{q-2}u=0,\quad \text{in}\ \ \Omega,\\
&u=0,\quad \text{on}\ \ \partial\Omega,
\end{cases}
\end{align*}where $\delta_{p}$ represents the Kirchhoff operator, $\alpha$ meets the requirements $0<\alpha<\frac{N-4}{p}$ and $2<p<\frac{N}{2}$, and $\Omega$ is a bounded domain with smooth boundary in $\mathbb{R}^{N}$ and satisfies $N\geq 5$. By employing a version of the Trudinger-Moser inequality with singular weights, we establish conditions under which the given system has multiple solutions for the variable exponent case.
